            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0173" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg71"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/429: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-06-24T18:00:00-04:00">June 24, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>149. One of our missions in Europe has reported in strict confidence that it has
                    learned the British Government intends to call a “general naval conference”,
                    including, among others, the Soviet Government, and that the latter has been
                    officially informed to this effect. Please cable us any confirmatory information
                    you may have been able discreetly to obtain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
